# Trusted-core paths require human code-owner review (ADR-0014, ADR-0017).
#
# Enforcement: the ruleset on main requires a pull request and a code-owner review. Repository
# administrators can bypass the review only through a pull request, never by pushing, because GitHub does
# not let an author approve their own pull request (issue #96). While there is one maintainer, the control
# for these paths is the explicit human instruction for each merge (ADR-0014). A second code owner added
# below makes the review rule bind without any other change.

# The trusted core: everything that runs in the engine or broker process (ADR-0017).
/core/                  @retroboot

# hyalOS: the monitor, the attestation programs and the evidence they are checked against (ADR-0130).
/hyalos-os/             @retroboot

# The workspace, the toolchain and the policies that every crate is built and checked under.
/Cargo.toml             @retroboot
/Cargo.lock             @retroboot
/rust-toolchain.toml    @retroboot
/clippy.toml            @retroboot
/deny.toml              @retroboot
/.gitleaks.toml         @retroboot
/LICENSE                @retroboot
/.cargo/                @retroboot

# The checks that enforce the layout and the size budget, and the CI that runs them.
/crates/xtask/          @retroboot
/.github/               @retroboot

# Decisions, product intent and the review rules themselves.
/docs/adr/              @retroboot
/docs/prd/              @retroboot
